    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0841" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H.00/1421⅝</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-24">December 24, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Yugoslav Ambassador called at his request and protested against the
                    continuing attacks being made in this country against General Mihailovitch.</p>
                <pb facs="0842" n="836" xml:id="pg836"/>
                <p>I said that, of course, this Government, during the time his King was here as
                    well as since, has shown the deepest sympathy for and interest in the welfare of
                    the Yugoslav people and their struggle for the restoration of their liberties. I
                    added that it might be well for him to speak with the officer in the European
                    Division on this matter and I would confer with this officer later today and
                    bring myself up to the minute on every detail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
